    <details><summary>How often should adults do brain teasers?</summary><p>Consistency matters more than duration. Around 10 to 15 minutes a day is a great target: one or two logic puzzles, a few riddles, or a single grid puzzle. A short daily habit keeps your reasoning sharp without feeling like homework, and it is easier to stick with than a long weekly session.</p></details>
